ports. All of them are licensed under Apache-2.0.

1. Laya
   https://github.com/NandhaKishorM/laya
   Copyright Convai Innovations and Laya contributors.
   The token sequence construction, question rendering, calibration and
   confidence calculation originate here.

2. laya-mlx (an MLX runtime for Laya)
   https://github.com/mizorewww/laya-mlx
   Copyright 2026 laya-mlx contributors.
   Source revision referenced: fc1df62828a3fedf4d8229fdac1cbd85f1cdf337

3. laya-mlx, mizchi's fork (adds the ONNX export and a TypeScript runtime)
   https://github.com/mizchi/laya-mlx
   Source revision referenced: dc3aa6b150cb861d0788fbd421cfd1303de4ed57
   `pipeline/laya.py` in this repository is a Python port of that fork's
   `web/packages/laya-web/src/{prompt,calibration,questions}.ts`, which are
   themselves a TypeScript port of Laya's `laya_mlx.common` / `laya_mlx.agent`.

   `web/src/laya/vendor/*.ts` are unmodified copies of that fork's
   `web/packages/laya-web/src/*.ts`, vendored because `@laya-mlx/web` is a
   private workspace package with no npm release. `web/vite.config.ts` also
   adapts that fork's plugin for dropping onnxruntime-web's unused wasm
   fallback asset.

Changes made in this repository (Apache-2.0 section 4(b)):
   - Reimplemented the above in Python against onnxruntime rather than MLX,
     Core ML or onnxruntime-web.
   - Added CUDA shared-library preloading so the CUDA execution provider is
     usable when those libraries come from `nvidia-*-cu12` pip packages
     installed in a user site directory.
   - Dropped the parts not needed here: the language router, application
     presets, email helpers, retry and action-cost handling.
   - Left the vendored TypeScript untouched; the browser app's own code lives
     outside that directory.

Model weights are downloaded separately from Hugging Face and are not included
in this repository:
   https://huggingface.co/mizchi/laya-multilingual-onnx  (Apache-2.0)
   derived from
   https://huggingface.co/convaiinnovations/laya-multilingual  (Apache-2.0)

